ONBOARDING

Onboarding = named script saved in workspace: quoted form walking user through
part of app, usually a ui/tour. Each user has own status per onboarding: new,
started or done. Status holds across chats.

- (onboardings) every onboarding as (name status about).
- (onboarding/read name) script form. Read before update.
- (onboarding/create name 'script [:about text]) save new one. Name is
  lower-case words joined by dashes. Quote script: unquoted form runs now and
  stores its result. Taken name errors.
- (onboarding/update name 'script [:about text]) replace script. Status kept.
- (onboarding/run name) evaluate script, return result. New user goes started.
- (onboarding/done name) mark user onboarded.
- (onboarding/done? name) t if user done, nil if not.

  (onboarding/create "welcome"
    '(ui/tour "welcome"
       '(:anchor "chats/new" :say "Start chat here" :until next)
       '(:say "Ask me anything"))
    :about "first look at app")

Give tour same id as onboarding. Finished tour sends "I finished the welcome
tour.": then (onboarding/done "welcome"). Skipped tour stays started.

RULES

- Check (onboarding/done? name) before running; do not rerun done one unasked.
- User asks how app works, and onboarding covers it: run that, do not improvise
  new tour.
- User asks to save walkthrough: create onboarding, not memory.
